      "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $x.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 4x =\nx(x^2 - 4)\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $x^2 - 4$ using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\nx(x^2 - 4) = x(x+2)(x-2)\n$$",
